  "body": "**The request (mkinney, 2026-11-15):** \"Can we have better docs on how to do 3+1 and continuous 4 axis milling? ... I want to use my microArc4.\" The user has a Tormach 770MX with a microARC 4 (machine file `assets/machines/tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch`).\n\nToday the pages are short: `multi-axis/indexed.md` (101 lines), `continuous-4-axis.md` (74 lines) and `machines-and-tcp.md` (83 lines). They name the microARC 4 only once or twice. There is no complete worked example.\n\nWanted: two step-by-step walkthroughs on the 770MX + microARC 4, each with a small committed demo project and images (see the example-images issue):\n1. **Indexed 3+1:** a part with features on several faces (for example a hex or a square bar with holes and pockets on four sides).\n   - Mount the part between centres or in a chuck on the A axis. Set the work offset on the rotary centreline (how to find it and probe it).\n   - Make one setup per index angle, or one setup with indexed operations. The guide says which one CamCraft prefers and why.\n   - How the post writes the A moves (unwind, clamp/unclamp if any, safe retract before an index).\n   - The checks: collision with the rotary and tailstock, and reach.\n2. **Continuous 4-axis:** wrapping (an engraving or a slot wrapped on a cylinder) and a rotary roughing or finishing pass.\n   - The operation choices, the feed-rate mode (inverse time or degrees per minute, and what the 770MX post writes), and the A-axis feed cap.\n   - Simulation and verify for 4-axis, and what a refusal means here.\n3. **Machine setup:** the microARC 4 machine file fields (A axis direction, limits, max rpm and feed), and the PathPilot settings to check before the first run.\n4. **Prove it out:** a dry run in the PathPilot Hub 770MX simulator with the 4th axis enabled. Which numbers to check: the A-axis direction and the wrap scale.\n\nClean room: CamCraft behaviour, Tormach's public documentation and general machining knowledge only.\n\nDone means: both walkthroughs are on the site with demo projects and images. Each posted program runs to M30 in the PathPilot Hub 770MX simulator with the microARC 4 (record the run on the issue). The pages link from the guide's Multi-axis section.\n",
